+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT */
+/*
+ * LG G7 ThinQ (Adreno 630): the full GPU driver for this port, glue written
+ * for it around the NativeAdreno core.
+ *
+ * bsd/dev/g7_gpu.c boots the GMU and powers GX (stages 2-4). With g7gpu=8 it
+ * then calls g7_adreno_bringup(), which here:
+ *   1. builds the GPU's SMMU context (page tables, kernel buffers for the SQE
+ *      microcode, ring, memptrs, scratch) with NativeAdrenoGpuContext;
+ *   2. programs the A630 registers (GMEM window at 16 MiB, clear of the
+ *      kernel buffers at 1-3 MiB), the ring and the SQE, starts the command
+ *      processor and runs CP_ME_INIT (NativeAdrenoRing, NativeAdrenoCpInit);
+ *   3. loads LG's zap shader through TrustZone and leaves secure mode;
+ *   4. attaches the submission object and publishes the Metal accelerator:
+ *      a service of class IOAcceleratorES with MetalPluginName
+ *      NativeAdrenoMetal, whose user clients speak the NativeAdreno ABI
+ *      (NativeAdrenoUserClient), as Turnip's Darwin backend expects, directly
+ *      or through the {magic, method} tunnel on any selector.
+ *
+ * The NativeAdreno*, ArmSmmu4K* and AdrenoPM4* files beside this one are MIT
+ * code from UniXNU (FFT-infra/Adreno650 a6xx-on-parity, UniXNU/ArmSmmu4K,
+ * UniXNU/AdrenoPM4), unchanged.
+ */
